  "limitations": [
    "GPU qualification is Windows Vulkan on the two named devices; Linux qualification here covers the portable native schedule only.",
    "Images are renderer readbacks. Scripted native UI/player/hosted and legacy ImGui layout tests do not qualify physical input or Avalonia editor usability.",
    "The schedule validates declared resource contracts and actual renderer bindings, not arbitrary shader memory accesses.",
    "NVRHI transitions and explicit cross-submission ordering remain required. No automatic pass parallelism, transient aliasing, deferred rendering, GI or performance improvement is claimed.",
    "Existing presentation lifetime policy remains: maintenance1 fences where available, bounded device-idle compatibility cleanup otherwise; the latter is not a formal presentation-completion proof.",
